            <div xml:id="trans1" xml:lang="en" type="translation" xml:space="preserve"><p>
<milestone unit="line" n="1"/> In the reign of our most godly and most pious master, Flavius Iustinianus, 
the eternal Augustus and Imperator, year 14, in the consulship of Flavius Iustinus, 
vir gloriosissimus, Phaophi …, of the auspicious fourth indiction, at Heracleopolis. 
I, Ioulios, priest of the Holy Church, son of Apanakios, mother Maria, 
from the village of Peene of the Heracleopolite nome, 
to Aurelia Manna daughter of … from Heracleopolis, greetings. 
I acknowledge that I have received from you, by hand, from (your) house, 
and have been paid in full the price of ten artabas of quality barley, 
(measured) by my own measure, and I will deliver them to you in good faith 
in the month of Pauni from the produce of the fifth indiction, with no delay 
and without any dispute. The deed is binding, 
and in reply to the formal question I assented. I, Ioulios, …
Back: Chirograph of Ioulios son of Apanakios, priest, from the village of Peene …
</p></div>
